            <title>0.79</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 02:17:33 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1791079809</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.79</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Blueprint cards in the Project pane can be reordered. Drag the grip on a card&#x27;s header to move it, and the new order is saved. The grip only appears when a project has more than one Blueprint.</li>
<li>Each Blueprint card has a collapse/expand button that shrinks it to its header. Addy remembers the choice per Blueprint on this Mac.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>The browser on your phone now gets its own phone-sized web view on the Mac, so the browser pane on the Mac no longer changes while you use it from your phone. It follows the Mac pane&#x27;s active tab and can show either a mobile page or a desktop-style page sized to your phone&#x27;s screen.</li>
<li>Taps and typing from your phone reach the page as real mouse and keyboard events. This makes sign-in forms inside cross-origin frames work, and sites that check for genuine input now accept them.</li>
<li>Your phone&#x27;s keyboard appears when a text field on the page has focus, including fields inside frames.</li>
<li>Browser shortcuts now take priority while a browser pane has keyboard focus. Cmd+T opens a new tab there instead of triggering the workspace terminal gesture, and Cmd+R, Cmd+W, Cmd+1–9, Cmd+Shift+[ / ], and zoom work the same way. Shift+Cmd+T remains the workspace-wide terminal gesture.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Internal Changes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Browser shortcut handling was consolidated into a single shared mapping, with new tests for shortcuts, Blueprint collapse, and Blueprint reordering.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
